!! Real-world example: Software release cycle

This example shows a full software release cycle across five phases: discovery, design, development, QA, and release. Tasks declare dependencies with `after`, show status (`done`, `active`, `crit`), and the `compact` display mode reduces row height for dense schedules.

```
%%{init: {"gantt": {"barHeight": 30, "displayMode": "compact"}}}%%
gantt
    dateFormat  YYYY-MM-DD
    axisFormat  %b %d
    title       v2.0 Release Cycle
    accTitle:   Software release cycle Gantt chart
    accDescr:   Full release schedule from discovery to launch

    %% ── Discovery ───────────────────────────────
    section Discovery
    Stakeholder interviews   :done,  d1, 2024-02-01, 5d
    Requirements workshop    :done,  d2, after d1, 3d
    Scope sign-off           :done,  d3, after d2, 2d

    %% ── Design ──────────────────────────────────
    section Design
    UX wireframes            :done,  ds1, after d3, 8d
    Design review            :done,  ds2, after ds1, 3d
    Design handoff           :done,  ds3, after ds2, 1d

    %% ── Development ─────────────────────────────
    section Development
    Backend API              :active, dev1, after ds3, 14d
    Frontend integration     :        dev2, after dev1, 10d
    Performance optimisation :        dev3, after dev2, 5d

    %% ── QA ──────────────────────────────────────
    section QA
    Regression suite         :crit,   qa1, after dev1, 7d
    UAT with stakeholders    :crit,   qa2, after dev2, 5d
    Bug-fix sprint           :        qa3, after qa1, 4d

    %% ── Release ─────────────────────────────────
    section Release
    Staging deployment       :        r1, after dev3, 2d
    Production deployment    :crit,   r2, after qa2, 1d
    Post-launch monitoring   :        r3, after r2, 5d
```

