---

!! Syntax

```
gantt
    dateFormat  YYYY-MM-DD
    axisFormat  %b %d
    title       My Project

    section Phase Name
    Task label   :status, id, startDate, duration
    Dependent    :status, id2, after id, duration
```

''Date formats:'' `YYYY-MM-DD`, `DD/MM/YYYY`, `MM-DD-YYYY`

''Axis formats:'' `%Y-%m-%d`, `%b %d`, `%d %b %Y` (strftime syntax)

|!Status keyword|!Meaning|
|`done`|Completed task (grey bar)|
|`active`|In-progress task (blue bar)|
|`crit`|Critical-path task (red bar)|
|`milestone`|Zero-duration milestone marker|

!! Tips

* Both `dateFormat` (input format) AND `axisFormat` (display format) are required for the x-axis labels to render correctly.
* Use `after taskId` for dependencies instead of hard-coding start dates — the chart stays consistent when durations change.
* `%%{init: {"gantt": {"displayMode": "compact"}}}%%` stacks multiple tasks in the same section row to reduce chart height.
* Section names label the rows inline — no additional legend is needed.
* See also: [[Timeline]] for a simpler chronological view, [[Kanban Board]] for in-flight task tracking.

